1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,464
Right this way, Mr. and Mrs. Stewart.

2
00:00:12,464 --> 00:00:15,640
Well, it's small, but clean.

3
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:23,824
Clean? You call this clean?

4
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:25,824
Have a nice stay.

5
00:00:25,824 --> 00:00:35,736
Thank you. I don't believe this.

6
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:41,692
Well, it isn't the Watermill Inn,

7
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:53,603
but let's get a look at the view.

8
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:56,581
How is the view?

9
00:00:56,581 --> 00:01:00,559
Great, if you enjoy looking at a parking lot.

10
00:01:00,559 --> 00:01:05,515
Well, maybe we'll see the view in the morning.

11
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:23,383
Right now, we should clean up this room.

12
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:26,361
Sorry, Marilyn.

13
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,694
Why should you be sorry?

14
00:01:29,694 --> 00:01:33,151
Well, the rain, the room, the view of the parking lot.

15
00:01:33,151 --> 00:01:37,295
It isn't the way I hoped it would be.

16
00:01:37,295 --> 00:01:39,873
Stop blaming yourself.

17
00:01:39,873 --> 00:01:47,207
After all, we're here, we're alone, we're together.

18
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:52,185
And I love you. Isn't that enough?

19
00:01:52,185 --> 00:01:53,163
It is for me,

20
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,140
but I wanted this weekend to be special for you.

21
00:01:56,140 --> 00:02:08,052
It is special. Happy anniversary.

22
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:11,030
It's still raining. I want to play tennis.

23
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:12,630
I want some breakfast.

24
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:15,833
Let's call room service and order a nice breakfast,

25
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:19,046
and then we'll figure out what to do today.

26
00:02:19,046 --> 00:02:24,832
Right. Would you give me room service, please?

27
00:02:24,832 --> 00:02:34,854
I beg your pardon? Oh, I see.

28
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:39,261
They don't have room service at Old Country Inn.

29
00:02:39,261 --> 00:02:43,060
Well, let's go down to the coffee shop.

30
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:45,788
They don't have a coffee shop.

31
00:02:45,788 --> 00:02:50,077
We can get our meals at Mrs. Montefiore's down the road.

32
00:02:50,077 --> 00:02:51,077
That's OK, honey.

33
00:02:51,077 --> 00:02:55,354
I love walking in the rain.

34
00:02:55,354 --> 00:02:59,474
Oh, you're being a really good sport about this, Marilyn,

35
00:02:59,474 --> 00:03:01,656
but I think we should face the truth.

36
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:02,090
What's that?

37
00:03:02,090 --> 00:03:05,534
This is not the way to spend our fifth anniversary.

38
00:03:05,534 --> 00:03:07,612
Well, what do you want to do?

39
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:11,489
Why don't we get in the car and drive home?

40
00:03:11,489 --> 00:03:13,567
Oh, Richard, it really isn't that bad.

41
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:18,145
Do you want to stick it out for the whole weekend?

42
00:03:18,145 --> 00:03:23,278
Well, I'll admit the room is uncomfortable.

43
00:03:23,278 --> 00:03:24,055
Uh-hum.

44
00:03:24,055 --> 00:03:28,229
And I do feel bad about your mother

45
00:03:28,229 --> 00:03:30,229
having to take care of the baby all weekend.

46
00:03:30,229 --> 00:03:31,895
Why don't we just check out?

47
00:03:31,895 --> 00:03:32,355
OK.

48
00:03:32,355 --> 00:03:43,347
Hello? Yes. Yes, this is she.

49
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:49,817
Oh, hello! How nice of you to remember us!

50
00:03:49,817 --> 00:03:52,281
Yes, my husband did call.

51
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:58,237
You do? Really? It won't be any trouble?

52
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:05,183
Oh, yes, I think we'd like that very much.

53
00:04:05,183 --> 00:04:08,911
Fifteen minutes! Thank you. Good-bye.

54
00:04:08,911 --> 00:04:16,105
You will never guess.

55
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:19,083
Uh ... I give up.

56
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:22,800
Mrs. Montefiore from the Watermill Inn.

57
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:28,238
What is she calling about?

58
00:04:28,238 --> 00:04:30,496
They have an opening.

59
00:04:30,496 --> 00:04:31,431
Someone just checked out.

60
00:04:31,431 --> 00:04:36,308
and Mrs. Montefiore has reserved the honeymoon suite for us.

61
00:04:36,308 --> 00:04:37,617
You're kidding!

62
00:04:37,617 --> 00:04:40,595
No. Isn't it wonderful?

63
00:04:40,595 --> 00:04:41,428
It's fantastic!

64
00:04:41,428 --> 00:04:45,884
Oh. Now all it has to do is stop raining.

65
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:48,884
Let's go.
